---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: Windows 95 - RetroOS Museum
description: Experience the revolutionary Windows 95 desktop with its iconic Start menu, taskbar, and classic applications.
bodyClass: win95-body
permalink: /os/windows-95/
---

{% block head %}
<!-- Windows 95 CSS -->
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/css/win95.css">
<style>
  /* Hide default header and footer for full desktop experience */
  body.win95-body header,
  body.win95-body footer {
    display: none;
  }

  body.win95-body main {
    padding: 0;
    max-width: none;
    margin: 0;
  }
</style>
{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
<!-- Windows 95 Desktop Environment -->
<div id="win95-desktop" class="win95-desktop" role="application" aria-label="Windows 95 Desktop">
  <!-- Desktop Icons Container -->
  <div id="desktop-icons" class="desktop-icons">
    <!-- Icons will be added by JavaScript -->
  </div>

  <!-- Taskbar -->
  <div id="win95-taskbar" class="win95-taskbar" role="navigation" aria-label="Taskbar">
    <!-- Start Button -->
    <button id="start-button" class="start-button" aria-label="Start Menu" aria-expanded="false" aria-haspopup="true">
      <img src="/assets/os/windows95/icons/windows-logo.svg" alt="" class="start-logo" width="16" height="16">
      <span class="start-text">Start</span>
    </button>

    <!-- Quick Launch (optional) -->
    <div class="quick-launch">
      <!-- Quick launch icons can be added here -->
    </div>

    <!-- Window Buttons Area -->
    <div id="taskbar-windows" class="taskbar-windows">
      <!-- Window buttons will be added dynamically -->
    </div>

    <!-- System Tray -->
    <div class="system-tray">
      <div class="tray-icons">
        <!-- Tray icons -->
        <span class="tray-icon" title="Volume">
          <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="currentColor">
            <path d="M8 3L4 6H1v4h3l4 3V3z"/>
            <path d="M11 5c.5.5 1 1.5 1 3s-.5 2.5-1 3"/>
          </svg>
        </span>
      </div>
      <div id="clock" class="clock" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true">
        <span id="clock-time">12:00 PM</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Start Menu (hidden by default) -->
  <div id="start-menu" class="start-menu" role="menu" aria-label="Start Menu" hidden>
    <div class="start-menu-banner">
      <span class="start-menu-logo">Windows<span class="win-95">95</span></span>
    </div>
    <div class="start-menu-items">
      <!-- Menu items will be populated by JavaScript -->
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Windows Container -->
  <div id="windows-container" class="windows-container">
    <!-- Windows will be added here by WindowManager -->
  </div>
</div>
{% endblock %}

{% block scripts %}
<!-- Core Systems -->
<script src="/assets/js/window-manager.js"></script>
<script src="/assets/js/menu-system.js"></script>
<script src="/assets/js/desktop.js"></script>

<!-- Windows 95 Specific -->
<script src="/assets/js/win95-taskbar.js"></script>
<script src="/assets/js/win95-start-menu.js"></script>
<script src="/assets/js/win95-desktop.js"></script>

<!-- Applications -->
<script src="/assets/js/apps/win95-notepad.js"></script>
<script src="/assets/js/apps/win95-paint.js"></script>
<script src="/assets/js/apps/win95-wordpad.js"></script>
<script src="/assets/js/apps/win95-minesweeper.js"></script>
<script src="/assets/js/apps/win95-solitaire.js"></script>
<script src="/assets/js/apps/win95-media-player.js"></script>
<script src="/assets/js/apps/win95-run.js"></script>
<script src="/assets/js/apps/win95-explorer.js"></script>
<script src="/assets/js/apps/win95-control-panel.js"></script>

<!-- Initialize Windows 95 -->
<script>
  // Wait for DOM to be ready
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', function() {
    // Initialize Windows 95 desktop
    if (typeof Win95Desktop !== 'undefined') {
      window.win95 = new Win95Desktop();
      window.win95.init();
    } else {
      console.error('Win95Desktop not loaded');
    }
  });
</script>
{% endblock %}
